{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.barEven_offset_insufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.barEven_offset_insufficient","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnInterfaceBarStructure.lean#L161-L170","doc":"A bar-**even** offset cannot restore bar-invariance unless it is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.pnWeighted_barEven_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.pnWeighted_barEven_iff","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnInterfaceBarStructure.lean#L142-L159","doc":"**The load-bearing statement: bar-even iff the offset is bar-ODD.**\n\nWhen `h ≠ 0`, the weighted p-n factor is fixed by the involution exactly when\n`ε' = -ε`.\n\nNote the direction.  A bar-*even* offset (`ε' = ε`) gives defect `-2ε·h`,\nwhich vanishes only in the trivial case `ε = 0`; symmetrising the weight is\ntherefore the wrong repair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.pnWeighted_bar_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.pnWeighted_bar_sub","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnInterfaceBarStructure.lean#L129-L140","doc":"**The bar defect of the weighted p-n factor.**\n\nApplying `bar` swaps `f_pp` and `f_nn` (by `fNN_eq_fPP_bar`) and sends the\noffset `ε` to `ε'`, so the image is `(1/2 + ε')·f_nn + (1/2 - ε')·f_pp`.  Its\ndifference from `fPN q ε` is `-(ε' + ε)·h`.\n\n`ε'` is taken as a parameter rather than computed: the conclusion depends only\non the relation between the offset and its image. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.fPN_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.fPN_eq","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnInterfaceBarStructure.lean#L120-L127","doc":"The weighted-mean form agrees with the explicit shifted form used in the\nproducers: `f_pn = z - (1/2 - ε)·h`.\n\nAt `ε = 0` this is `z - h/2`, the `δ = 0` factor; at `ε = δ/4` it is the\ncolour-tube-weighted `z - h(1/2 - δ/4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.strictPn_eq_barSymmetriser","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.strictPn_eq_barSymmetriser","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnInterfaceBarStructure.lean#L114-L118","doc":"**The `δ = 0` p-n factor is the bar symmetriser.**\n`z - h/2 = (z(q) + z(q⁻¹))/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.fNN_eq_fPP_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.fNN_eq_fPP_bar","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnInterfaceBarStructure.lean#L108-L112","doc":"`f_nn` is the bar image of `f_pp`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.barZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.barZ","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnInterfaceBarStructure.lean#L93-L106","doc":"**The p-p and n-n factors are bar conjugates.**  `z(q⁻¹) = z(q) - h(q)`,\nso the two like-flavour bonds form a single orbit of `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.fPN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.fPN","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnInterfaceBarStructure.lean#L88-L91","doc":"The p-n bond factor with weight offset `ε`:\n`(1/2 + ε)·f_pp + (1/2 - ε)·f_nn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.fNN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.fNN","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnInterfaceBarStructure.lean#L85-L86","doc":"The n-n bond factor: a negative crossing contributes `z - h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.fPP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.fPP","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnInterfaceBarStructure.lean#L82-L83","doc":"The p-p bond factor: a positive crossing contributes `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.heckeH","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnInterfaceBarStructure.lean#L79-L80","doc":"The Hecke skein parameter, `h = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.markovZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure.markovZ","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnInterfaceBarStructure.lean#L76-L77","doc":"The Markov parameter in convention D, `z = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}